{%- comment -%}
  Organization + WebSite structured data, emitted once per page from the footer.

  WHY THE FOOTER: the Organization's sameAs profiles are the social links the
  footer already renders as blocks, so they are read from that data rather than
  retyped into a second place that could drift. Horizon emitted Organization
  from sections/header.liquid, which is disabled in this theme's header group —
  so without this the redesign shipped with no entity markup at all.

  WebSite/SearchAction declares the on-site search endpoint, which is what makes
  a sitelinks search box possible. /search is real and takes ?q=, so this
  describes something that genuinely exists.

  alternateName / description (SEO audit 2026-09-30): the brand trades as
  CROOKSLDN, Crooks London and Crooks (@crooksldn). Declaring the alternates
  lets search engines and AI tools resolve all three to one entity. The
  description is a fallback used only while the shop description is blank.

  Entity graph (Promptd SEO/GEO audit 2026-10, findings A1, G2, G10): the
  Organization now carries the legal name the business trades under, the
  CROOKSLDN Brand that every product points at by @id, and the store-wide
  returns policy, so search engines and answer engines can tie products,
  brand, company and policy together instead of reading loose objects.

  The returns facts mirror the refund policy and the Terms page: 14 days from
  delivery, sent back by post, the shopper pays postage on a change-of-mind
  return, faulty or wrong items come back free. Shown to Google at
  organization level, which it reads for every product on the site. If the
  policy changes, change these lines with it.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign crk_social_hosts = 'instagram.com,tiktok.com,facebook.com,youtube.com,x.com,twitter.com,pinterest.com,linkedin.com,threads.net,threads.com,snapchat.com,tumblr.com,soundcloud.com,spotify.com' | split: ','
  assign crk_same = ''
  for block in section.blocks
    for i in (1..6)
      case i
        when 1
          assign crk_u = block.settings.url_1
        when 2
          assign crk_u = block.settings.url_2
        when 3
          assign crk_u = block.settings.url_3
        when 4
          assign crk_u = block.settings.url_4
        when 5
          assign crk_u = block.settings.url_5
        when 6
          assign crk_u = block.settings.url_6
      endcase
      comment
        Off-site profile links only: skip internal routes, mailto and the
        shop's own domain.
      endcomment
      comment
        sameAs means "another profile of THIS organisation", so it is limited to
        known social hosts. Without the allowlist the footer's CASE 001 link —
        a game on base44 — was being published as a CROOKSLDN profile.
      endcomment
      assign crk_is_social = false
      for host in crk_social_hosts
        if crk_u contains host
          assign crk_is_social = true
          break
        endif
      endfor
      if crk_is_social
            if crk_same == ''
              assign crk_same = crk_u
            else
              unless crk_same contains crk_u
                assign crk_same = crk_same | append: '|' | append: crk_u
              endunless
            endif
      endif
    endfor
  endfor
  assign crk_same_list = crk_same | split: '|'

  assign crk_org_desc = shop.description | strip_html | strip_newlines
  if crk_org_desc == blank
    assign crk_org_desc = 'CROOKSLDN (Crooks London) is a streetwear label making heavyweight fleece, denim, graphic T-shirts and accessories, sold online at crooksldn.com.'
  endif

  comment
    SearchAction needs the literal {search_term_string} placeholder. A brace
    inside a Liquid tag argument is read as a delimiter and the theme is
    rejected at upload, so it is assembled from single-character variables.
  endcomment
  assign crk_ob = '{'
  assign crk_cb = '}'
  assign crk_search_template = shop.url | append: '/search?q=' | append: crk_ob | append: 'search_term_string' | append: crk_cb
-%}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Organization",
  "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '#organization' | json }},
  "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
  "legalName": "Crooks Clothing Company Ltd",
  "alternateName": ["Crooks London", "Crooks"],
  "url": {{ shop.url | json }},
  {% if settings.logo != blank %}"logo": {{ settings.logo | image_url: width: 512 | prepend: 'https:' | replace: 'https:https:', 'https:' | json }},{% endif %}
  "brand": {
    "@type": "Brand",
    "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '#brand' | json }},
    "name": {{ shop.name | json }}{% if settings.logo != blank %},
    "logo": {{ settings.logo | image_url: width: 512 | prepend: 'https:' | replace: 'https:https:', 'https:' | json }}{% endif %}
  },
  "hasMerchantReturnPolicy": {
    "@type": "MerchantReturnPolicy",
    "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '#return-policy' | json }},
    "url": {{ shop.url | append: '/policies/refund-policy' | json }},
    "applicableCountry": "GB",
    "returnPolicyCountry": "GB",
    "returnPolicyCategory": "https://schema.org/MerchantReturnFiniteReturnWindow",
    "merchantReturnDays": 14,
    "returnMethod": "https://schema.org/ReturnByMail",
    "customerRemorseReturnFees": "https://schema.org/ReturnShippingFees",
    "itemDefectReturnFees": "https://schema.org/FreeReturn"
  },
  "description": {{ crk_org_desc | json }},
  {% if crk_same_list.size > 0 %}"sameAs": [{% for u in crk_same_list %}{% unless forloop.first %},{% endunless %}{{ u | json }}{% endfor %}],{% endif %}
  "contactPoint": {
    "@type": "ContactPoint",
    "contactType": "customer support",
    "email": {{ shop.email | json }},
    "areaServed": "GB"
  }
}
</script>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebSite",
  "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '#website' | json }},
  "url": {{ shop.url | json }},
  "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
  "alternateName": ["Crooks London", "Crooks"],
  "inLanguage": {{ request.locale.iso_code | default: 'en' | json }},
  "publisher": { "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '#organization' | json }} },
  "potentialAction": {
    "@type": "SearchAction",
    "target": {
      "@type": "EntryPoint",
      "urlTemplate": {{ crk_search_template | json }}
    },
    "query-input": "required name=search_term_string"
  }
}
</script>
